From: Joshua S. Day <haxmeister@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix qw backslash warning on Perl 5.44

Perl 5.44 warns when a bare backslash in a qw() list escapes the
following whitespace. t/Net-WebSocket-HTTP.t uses Test::FailWarnings,
so the warning adds a failing test and prevents a normal installation.

Keep the backslash test case, but spell that value explicitly outside
qw().

---
 t/Net-WebSocket-HTTP.t | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/t/Net-WebSocket-HTTP.t b/t/Net-WebSocket-HTTP.t
--- a/t/Net-WebSocket-HTTP.t
+++ b/t/Net-WebSocket-HTTP.t
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ use Test::FailWarnings;
 use Test::Exception;
 
 my @invalid = (
-    ( map { "ha${_}he" } qw~ ( ) < > @ ; : \ " / [ ] ? = { } ~ ),
+    ( map { "ha${_}he" } (qw~ ( ) < > @ ; : ~, '\\', qw~ " / [ ] ? = { } ~) ),
 );
 
 plan tests => 5 + @invalid;
